    {"kind":"note","x":34,"y":44,"id":"ranger-walt","by":"ranger","name":"Nailed to the pole","text":["Walt: your line hums at night past the crossroads, and it has no business humming. Thought you should know."]},
    {"kind":"note","x":38,"y":45,"id":"walt-n14","by":"walt","name":"Nailed to the pole","text":["Ranger: I know. It's dead and it hums. On green nights the whole line sings, town to the old cabin.","Pulled a span down here after a storm. A month on there was copper lying on the ground again, new. Nobody strung it. W.P."]},
    {"kind":"note","x":46,"y":42,"id":"walt-n16","by":"walt","name":"Nailed to the pole","text":["N-16, end of the line. Scratched this with a shard, the ranger's trick. Only shows when the sky's green.","Green nights, the dead wire sings from here to town. I climbed it on a green night. There is nothing on it.","Tag's off this pole. Whoever finds it, keep it. W.P."],"when":"aurora","faint":"Scratched into the paper with something sharp. The scratches only show when the sky is green."},
    {"kind":"note","x":33,"y":60,"id":"walt-truck","by":"walt","name":"In the glove box","text":["Truck log, the night of the answer. Up N-16 at eleven, after the hum. Tower sent at 11:40. Wire jumped in my hands.","Woods lit up to the north like a town. Truck dead where I left it. Don't remember the walk home. W.P."]},
    {"kind":"note","x":32,"y":60,"id":"barlow-wiper","by":"barlows","name":"Under the wiper","text":["In the rain, white crayon shows on the wet paper, pale on grey:","WE WALKED OUT TODAY, ALL THREE OF US. NOBODY SAW US GO. SECRET. W."],"when":"rain","faint":"The paper looks blank, and feels waxy. Wet, it might show something."}
  ],
